# perlmutter
Each node contains 2 sockets, each containing an AMD EPYC 7763 processor. Each
processor has 64 physical cores, and each core has 2 hardware threads (logical
CPUs). Each processor has 4 NUMA domains. For details, see Perlmutter
architecture.

Socket 1 has physical cores 0 to 63, and socket 2 has physical cores 64 to 127.
Core 0 has 2 hardware threads, with the logical CPUs numbered as 0 and 128;
Core 1 has logical CPUs of 1 and 129, and so on. When OMP_PLACES is set to
"cores", each OpenMP thread binds to one core; And when OMP_PLACES is set to
"threads", each OpenMP thread binds to one logical CPU.

